      en: "Schoorlse Duinen is a dune area in North Holland near Schoorl. Spanning about 1,800 hectares, it is one of the widest dune areas in the Netherlands. It stretches from the North Sea to the polder. Dunes reach heights up to 60 meters. The area formed over centuries from wind-blown sand. Vegetation includes sea buckthorn, sea sandwort, and lichens. Rare plants like sea holly thrive in dune valleys. It is an important breeding site for woodlark and northern wheatear. Hiking and biking trails cross the landscape. The visitor center covers dune formation and ecology.",
